{% comment %}
  One row of the event list.

  Extracted so the two sources -- a Seminars collection and hand-authored
  blocks -- render identically. Duplicating the markup in both branches is how
  the fallback quietly stops matching the real thing.

    city        string, required
    date        string, already formatted for display
    focus       string, blank renders the TBA state
    price       string, already money-formatted
    target      href for the fallback link. Ignored when a product is passed
    sold_out    boolean. Renders a flat row with no panel
    cue         buy button text, defaults to "Reserve"
    attrs       block.shopify_attributes, or blank in collection mode
    product     the product object, when there is one
    venue       string, e.g. "Example Gym -- Example City"
    address     string, one line
    map         url
    time        string, already formatted -- "12:00 PM – 5:00 PM"

  THE ROW OPENS INSTEAD OF NAVIGATING. The product page held four facts this
  list did not -- venue, address, map, hours -- and a page load to read four
  facts is a context switch at the moment someone has decided to buy.

  <details>/<summary>, NOT a JavaScript accordion: it opens with no script, is
  keyboard operable and announced as expandable for free, and Ctrl+F opens a
  closed panel. A hand-built accordion gets none of that without work.

  THE ROW IS NO LONGER A LINK. An <a> cannot contain a <form>, which forced the
  old choice between the product page and /cart/{variant}:1, neither reaching
  checkout. A <summary> carries no such restriction.

  PRODUCT IS PASSED AS AN OBJECT, breaking this snippet's rule that every value
  arrives resolved: `{% form 'product' %}` needs the object.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign has_details = false
  if venue != blank or address != blank or map != blank or time != blank
    assign has_details = true
  endif

  assign can_buy = false
  if product != blank and sold_out != true
    assign can_buy = true
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Nothing to reveal and nothing to sell: a control that opens onto an empty box
  is worse than none, so it falls back to the flat row, as sold-out does.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if sold_out or has_details == false and can_buy == false -%}
  <div class="suf-semrow suf-semrow--flat" {{ attrs }}>
    <div class="suf-semrow__line">
      {%- render 'suf-semcells', city: city, date: date, focus: focus, price: price -%}
      {%- if sold_out -%}
        <span class="suf-semrow__focus suf-semrow__focus--tba">Sold out</span>
      {%- elsif target != blank -%}
        <a class="suf-semrow__cue" href="{{ target }}">
          {{- cue | default: 'Reserve' | escape }}
          <span class="suf-semrow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </a>
      {%- else -%}
        <span></span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- else -%}
  <details class="suf-semrow" {{ attrs }}>
    <summary class="suf-semrow__line">
      {%- render 'suf-semcells', city: city, date: date, focus: focus, price: price -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        aria-hidden: <summary> already announces expanded/collapsed, so naming
        the state again would have a screen reader say it twice.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        "Details", not the `cue` setting -- the cue is the BUY word and labels
        the button inside the panel. "Reserve" on a control that only opens is
        the same broken promise the old row made.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="suf-semrow__cue">
        Details
        <span class="suf-semrow__chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </span>
    </summary>

    <div class="suf-semrow__panel">
      {%- if has_details -%}
        <dl class="suf-semrow__facts">
          {%- if venue != blank -%}
            <div class="suf-semrow__fact">
              <dt>Where</dt>
              <dd>
                {{ venue | escape }}
                {%- if address != blank -%}
                  <span class="suf-semrow__addr">{{ address | escape }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  A new tab: someone measuring the gym against an airport is
                  mid-purchase, and taking the page away loses the sale. rel is
                  not optional -- without noopener the opened page gets a
                  handle on this one.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- if map != blank -%}
                  <a
                    class="suf-semrow__map"
                    href="{{ map }}"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  >
                    Open in Maps
                    <span class="suf-visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span>
                  </a>
                {%- endif -%}
              </dd>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if time != blank -%}
            <div class="suf-semrow__fact">
              <dt>Hours</dt>
              <dd>{{ time | escape }}</dd>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </dl>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if can_buy -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          A REAL add-to-cart, straight to checkout. The date is not a choice
          here -- this row IS the date -- so unlike the bundles there is no
          seminar property to carry: the variant says which seminar it is.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- form 'product', product, class: 'suf-semrow__form' -%}
          <input
            type="hidden"
            name="id"
            value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"
          >
          <input type="hidden" name="return_to" value="/checkout">
          <button type="submit" class="suf-btn suf-btn--primary" name="add">
            {{- cue | default: 'Reserve' | escape }} &middot; {{ price -}}
          </button>
        {%- endform -%}
      {%- elsif target != blank -%}
        <a class="suf-btn suf-btn--primary" href="{{ target }}">
          {{- cue | default: 'Reserve' | escape -}}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </details>
{%- endif -%}
